        },
        "visual_elements": {
          "main_visual": "Two parallel service lanes, each with its own account and sign-in step. A user moves from the first lane to the second."
        },
        "required_images": [],
        "notes": "Imagine a user who works across two services, each with its own sign-in step. The first task is complete, but moving to the next service interrupts the journey with another account interaction. This example illustrates the kind of friction the proposal is trying to address; it is not a claim about how often our users experience it.\n\nThe proposal asks whether some of those repeated steps could be removed. Let us look at what a shared login would need to do."
