        "visual_elements": {
          "main_visual": "One shared account node at left connects to three aligned service nodes at right. Distinguish account recognition from service access with subtle connector styling; no implementation stack."
        },
        "required_images": [],
        "notes": "The basic idea is that a user has one account that connected services recognize. If a service can accept an existing sign-in session, the user may reach that service without repeating the whole sign-in process. That is the mechanism behind the possible time saving.\n\nThis diagram describes the proposal at the level of experience and identity. It does not choose a protocol, an identity provider or a migration approach. We also need to decide what recognition of an account allows the user to access. Those are related questions, but we should keep them visible as separate responsibilities."
